Todo verificado. Reporte de aceptación:

## Resumen

**Entregado:**
- `tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py` — herramienta que parchea offsets de section_3 del stock a `b .` (FE E7), con verificación de código-Thumb-plausible y verificación de diffs
- `build/ReChord_V0.19_map_USB.IMG` — hangs en {0x0300016c WriteData_To_Flash, 0x0300024e MscTestUnitReady, 0x03000aba main2_entry}
- `build/ReChord_V0.19_map_misc.IMG` — hangs en {0x03000296, 0x030004f4, 0x03000546, 0x03000a72, 0x03000a74}
- `build/ReChord_V0.19_map_appstart.IMG` — hang en {0x0300710a application_start}

**Verificación por IMG** (independiente del tool): cada uno difiere del stock SOLO en los pares FE E7 patcheados (6/10/2 bytes), trailer 0x1EA1C309 preservado. Todos los offsets verificados contenían código Thumb real antes del patch. El offset 0x03000162 (bx lr stock) se excluyó de los grupos como indica la tarea. El modo standalone (`-n/--offsets/-o`) funciona y rechaza offsets que apuntan a padding (byte 0x00).

```acceptance-report
{
  "criteriaSatisfied": [
    {
      "id": "criterion-1",
      "status": "satisfied",
      "evidence": "tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py implements exactly the requested scope: stock IMG + 'b .' (FE E7) hangs at given section_3 RAM offsets, with pre-patch code-plausibility check and post-patch diff verification. --build-all produces the 3 requested IMGs; standalone CLI mode also works; nothing else was changed."
    }
  ],
  "changedFiles": [
    "tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py"
  ],
  "testsAddedOrUpdated": [
    "manual verification via python one-liners (not committed as test files)"
  ],
  "commandsRun": [
    {
      "command": "python tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py --build-all",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "Built map_USB (3 hangs), map_misc (5 hangs), map_appstart (1 hang); each verified to differ from stock only at the patched 2-byte windows"
    },
    {
      "command": "python -c independent diff/trailer check",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "map_USB: 6 diff bytes/3 hang sites; map_misc: 10/5; map_appstart: 2/1; trailer 0x1ea1c309 preserved in all"
    },
    {
      "command": "python tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py -n map_test --offsets 0x030004f4 -o build/ReChord_V0.19_standalone_test.IMG",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "Standalone CLI mode patches only the given offset (diffs at 0x81f08/0x81f09 only)"
    },
    {
      "command": "python tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py -n neg --offsets 0x03000100 -o build/neg.IMG",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "Rejects offset pointing at 0x00 padding with ValueError (refuses to patch data)"
    }
  ],
  "validationOutput": [
    "Pre-patch bytes at all 10 patched offsets are plausible Thumb code (push/ldr/etc.), e.g. 0x0300016c -> 2de9f04f, 0x03000aba -> 2de9f04f, 0x0300710a -> bdf80cc0",
    "0x03000162 confirmed bx lr (70 47) in stock and excluded from all groups per task",
    "Per-IMG diff verification passed: map_USB [0x81b80,0x81b81,0x81c62,0x81c63,0x824ce,0x824cf], map_misc [0x81caa..0x82489], map_appstart [0x88b1e,0x88b1f]",
    "All hang sites are FE E7 pairs; trailer 0x1EA1C309 identical to stock in all 3 IMGs"
  ],
  "residualRisks": [
    "Empirical mapping requires flashing each IMG; a hang at an offset called during boot would freeze the device at power-on (recoverable by reflashing stock, verified working on device)",
    "0x03000a72/0x03000a74 are 2 bytes apart, so their hang windows are contiguous (0x82486-0x82489) — both become 'b .' as intended"
  ],
  "noStagedFiles": true,
  "diffSummary": "One new file: tools/make_v019_dispatch_map.py (script). Three build artifacts produced but not committed (build/ is gitignored). No stock/firmware sources modified.",
  "reviewFindings": [
    "no blockers"
  ],
  "manualNotes": "Artifacts: build/ReChord_V0.19_map_USB.IMG, build/ReChord_V0.19_map_misc.IMG, build/ReChord_V0.19_map_appstart.IMG. Flash each and press the 5 menu items (file browser, media library, music, settings x2) to map which offset each feature uses. Restore stock by reflashing the stock IMG if a hang is on the boot path."
}
```

